Input: {"question": "When was Ralph Cole elected to the Ohio House of Representatives?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d00", "start": 0, "end": 55, "text": "Ralph Cole (Ohio representative) Ralph Dayton Cole, Jr."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d00", "start": 56, "end": 153, "text": "(June 12, 1914 – September 2, 1999) was a Republican member of the Ohio House of Representatives."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d00", "start": 154, "end": 373, "text": "A graduate of Williams College and Case Western Reserve University, he was originally elected to an at-large district in 1954 to represent Hancock County, Ohio, and he would go on to serve seven more terms in the House."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d00", "start": 374, "end": 538, "text": "Throughout his tenure in the legislature, Cole served on various committees in leadership positions, most notably as chairman of the State and Government Committee."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d00", "start": 539, "end": 607, "text": "In 1968, Cole was appointed to a judicial seat for the Ohio District"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d01", "start": 0, "end": 649, "text": "Congress 1954 Shooting in the House Chamber A Century of Women in Congress Civil Rights Documentaries House Collection Objects House Pages Institutional Interviews September 11, 2001 Watergate World War II Featured Search All Oral History Media National History Day 2025: Rights and Responsibilities in History Kids in the House Download or Request our Publications Primary Source Sets Student Guides Tools for Teaching with Primary Sources Lesson Plans Education Fact Sheets Time for a Tour: Visiting the People’s House Glossary Timeline Featured Resources for National History Day Records Search Researching the House: Official Records Researching"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d01", "start": 651, "end": 773, "text": "Ralph Cole was elected to the Ohio House of Representatives in 1972, marking a significant moment in his political career."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d01", "start": 774, "end": 862, "text": "This election came at a time of increasing political engagement and reform in the state."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 0, "end": 62, "text": "member of the Ohio House of Representatives from 1900 to 1904."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 63, "end": 185, "text": "Cole was elected as a Republican to the Fifty-ninth, Sixtieth, and Sixty-first Congresses (March 4, 1905 – March 3, 1911)."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 186, "end": 273, "text": "He was an unsuccessful candidate for renomination in 1910 to the Sixty-second Congress."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 274, "end": 344, "text": "He resumed the practice of law in Findlay, Toledo, and Columbus, Ohio."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 345, "end": 411, "text": "Legal adviser to the Comptroller of the Currency in 1912 and 1913."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 412, "end": 506, "text": "Cole served as chairman of the speakers' bureau for the Republican National Committee in 1916."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d02", "start": 507, "end": 603, "text": "He was also chosen as a delegate to the Republican National Conventions in 1916, 1924, and 1928."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 0, "end": 28, "text": "Ohio Northern University ) ."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 29, "end": 113, "text": "[ 5 ] From 1897 to 1899 , Cole served as the deputy clerk of Hancock County , Ohio ."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 114, "end": 218, "text": "[ 1 ] While working in the clerk 's office , he studied law in preparation for a career as an attorney ."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 219, "end": 297, "text": "[ 1 ] Cole was admitted to the bar in 1900 and commenced practice in Findlay ."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 298, "end": 423, "text": "[ 1 ] Political career [ edit ] A Republican , Cole served as member of the Ohio House of Representatives from 1900 to 1904 ."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d03", "start": 424, "end": 454, "text": "[ 1 ] In 1904 , he was elected"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d04", "start": 0, "end": 25, "text": "also served in Congress ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d04", "start": 26, "end": 197, "text": "A native of Vanlue , Ohio , Cole was raised and educated in Findlay , graduated from Findlay College in 1896 , then attended Ada College ( now Ohio Northern University ) ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d04", "start": 198, "end": 335, "text": "He worked as deputy clerk of Hancock County , Ohio while studying law , and he was admitted to the bar in 1900 and practiced in Findlay ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d04", "start": 336, "end": 479, "text": "In addition to practicing law , Cole was active in politics as a Republican and served in the Ohio House of Representatives from 1900 to 1904 ."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0290-88ccccab6be3:d04", "start": 480, "en